!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/validate/valid/a-record-fields-value-is-read-against-its-type-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/validate-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    The kernel's `record_field.value` is typed `type!`: read as data, a record field's `value` is read against the
    type its own `type` names, so `5` beside `type: integer` is an integer and the record field is valid.
    """
  valid: _
}
